## What the author owns

Who says what around the notice table beyond the protected lines; the documentary room's ink and boxes; the address hall's crowd; the semifinal's tactics inside the facts (Fiske's complete model; the long minute; the hip); the corridor confrontation's wording; the carriages' order and weather. Humor in the back room: Karis on the floor, ink to the knuckle, finding it "the *best* way to describe a good afternoon."

