editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md-198-- Timber vs stone: four bursts on timber cost what three did on stone — a third more work, or about a quarter less per burst. "Four free" at the baseline.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md-199-- Lira's record: three wins on day 28, eight by day 32 ("eight and nil"), nine by day 34.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md-200-- Lira's Fenmark Arbiter reading took "about a minute and a half" — NEW CANON (no earlier book states it); the registrar's clerk "most of two minutes" (ch9).
