editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:211:**Fragments & progression.** Five confirmed; no change. Wind: four free on sprung timber, fifth billed (about a third cheaper than stone); landing beat unchanged; baseline 1–5 within one brass, sixth wide and long. Iron read: blind to Lattice, silently; rule in both books; partial correction (builder's weight, pupils only); baseline 11/12, cold 12/12. Pressure withheld at the plate. Compression untested on a floor that answers (ringed). Ember off the floor by agreement with Karis. Tide anomaly not mentioned.
